<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Privacydataprotection Policy - AJSMR</title><style>body{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0;background:#f5f6f8;color:#222;line-height:1.65}.container{max-width:1050px;margin:35px auto;padding:0 20px}.card{background:#fff;border-radius:8px;padding:32px;box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.08)}h1{margin-top:0;color:#222;font-size:30px}h2{font-size:21px;margin-top:28px;color:#333}li{margin:8px 0}.note{background:#f0f4f8;padding:14px 16px;border-left:4px solid #555;margin:20px 0}.small{font-size:13px;color:#666}</style></head><body><div class="container"><div class="card"><h1>Privacy & Data Protection Policy</h1><div class="note">AJSMR collects and processes personal information needed to operate submission, peer-review, editorial and publication workflows.</div><h2>Information Collected</h2><p>Depending on interaction with the journal, AJSMR may collect names, affiliations, email addresses, ORCID identifiers where provided, manuscript information, reviewer information, correspondence and account information.</p><h2>Purposes of Processing</h2><p>Information may be used to receive and manage manuscripts, conduct peer review, communicate decisions, invite reviewers, publish article metadata, manage accounts, respond to enquiries and administer the journal.</p><h2>Confidentiality</h2><p>Manuscripts and confidential peer-review information should not be disclosed to unauthorized persons.</p><h2>Data Minimization</h2><p>The journal should collect information reasonably necessary for submission, review, publication, communication and legitimate administration.</p><h2>Security</h2><p>The publisher should use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure or loss.</p><h2>Published Information</h2><p>Author names, affiliations and article metadata may form part of the scholarly record. Private contact information should not be published unless appropriate.</p><h2>Retention</h2><p>Editorial records may need to be retained for administration and integrity of the scholarly record.</p><h2>Third-Party Services</h2><p>Where external services are used for hosting, manuscript management, DOI registration or integrity screening, relevant data handling should be appropriately governed.</p><h2>Privacy Enquiries</h2><p>Privacy enquiries may be directed to the journal or publisher using the current contact details displayed on the AJSMR website.</p><p class="small">AJSMR local testing version. Final wording should be confirmed against actual journal practices before live publication.</p></div></div></body></html>